Z||000008||Carrolles||04-02-2001||12:07 PM||||With the trans in neutral and one wheel off the ground, that wheel should turn freely in either direction.  <P>With both wheels off the ground, trans in neutral, either wheel should turn independently of each other in either direction.  You might feel a little drag causing the wheels to turn in opposite directions but if you hold one wheel the other should turn freely in either direction.<P>Trans in gear and one wheel off the ground you should not be able to turn the elevated wheel.<P>Trans in gear and both wheels off the ground.  When you turn one wheel the other turns an equal amount in the opposite direction.<P>I'm not quite sure of what you are describing.  Give it another try.<P>It sounds like you have a slightly warped rotor that is grabbing the brake pads as the wheel turns to the high spot.||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||04-02-2001||12:08 PM||||i just tried it jacking my V6 4spd. with both in the air both spin freely, with only one up, each one still spins free. Im not sure but could be you have a prob in the final gears/spyders. Im not a tranny person, but I tried.<P>he says caliper is clear off and still locks up, so think that takes out any brake prob<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||1
